 "texts": {
  "fields": [
   {
    "name": "target_locations",
    "description": "During the video cycle, identify which container descends over each requested cube colour. Follow those containers continuously across the shuffle frames, including exchanges between identical-looking containers. Write their final front-image silhouette centres as [u,v] pixel pairs in requested colour order. Do not infer identity from the final arrangement alone or assume a container returned to its original identity because the arrangement repeats. Carry this list unchanged at every act cycle. e.g. [[131,71],[117,146]]",
    "annotation": "An ordered list of [u,v] front-image container-centre locations, in pixels, at the end of the demonstration, one for each requested cube colour in instruction order. Identify the container that originally covered each requested cube and follow its continuous motion through every shuffle; record its final location, not the cube's original location. Include no distractors. Use the centre of the entire visible container silhouette consistently. Set this list at the video cycle and retain it throughout execution, including after a selected container moves. e.g. [[131,71],[117,146]]",
    "value_type": "other",
    "tolerance": 3.0
   },
   {
    "name": "completed_lifts",
    "description": "Initialize to zero at the video cycle. Increment once when this cycle's motion frames show the next requested container rising with the closed gripper from grasp height to approximately 0.20 m TCP height. The container must move with the hand; a newly exposed cube supports confirmation. Count the observed lift, not a lift you are about to command. Do not increment for a static elevated grasp, a downward return, an open-hand withdrawal, or a grasp closure at low height. If the motion executes no steps, retain the count. Otherwise retain the incoming value unless this successful new lift is observed. e.g. 1",
    "annotation": "Number of requested containers already lifted successfully in instruction order. Initialize to zero at the video cycle. Increment at the first act cycle showing the selected container carried upward from grasp height to approximately 0.20 m TCP height with the gripper closed. Do not increment for closing at grasp height, returning a container, withdrawing with an open gripper, or continuing to hold an already-counted container. Retain the count otherwise. e.g. 1",
    "value_type": "count"
   },
   {
    "name": "final_layout_keyframe",
    "description": "During the video cycle, select the last shown frame of the settled final arrangement in which the requested containers are unobstructed and write its frame label. Carry that label unchanged at every act cycle. Do not replace it with an execution frame or update it when a completed container is returned. Its geometry is a reference only for containers that have not subsequently moved. e.g. V113",
    "annotation": "The label of the last shown demonstration frame of the settled final arrangement in which the requested containers are unobstructed. Set at the video cycle and retain unchanged throughout execution, including after a selected container is returned. This frame preserves reference geometry for targets that have not subsequently moved, not the current pose of returned containers. e.g. V113",
    "value_type": "keyframe"
   }
